route: visual

---

[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The Ace Pro 2 has a lot of useful features, some&nbsp; of which are hidden. the many features can be a&nbsp;&nbsp; bit overwhelming at first. That\'s why today&nbsp; in a few simple steps I\'ll explain everything&nbsp;&nbsp; you have to know to achieve great results with&nbsp; the Ace Pro 2. To give this video a little more&nbsp;&nbsp; structure, it is divided into 20 parts that&nbsp; correspond to the most important features.'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Let\'s start with the body of the Ace Pro 2 and&nbsp; we should take a closer look at it, also because&nbsp;&nbsp; several parts can be removed. A particular&nbsp; highlight of the Ace Pro 2 is the flip-up&nbsp;&nbsp; display. It makes the Ace Pro 2 the perfect&nbsp; camera for filming yourself. The display has&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a locking mechanism. To fold it up, press the two&nbsp; small buttons on the left and right side. Then you&nbsp;&nbsp; can fold up the display completely. Of course, you&nbsp; can also use it at any other angle, for example to&nbsp;&nbsp; control the framing when looking at the camera&nbsp; from above. And you can also use the display to&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'position the camera at a certain angle looking&nbsp; upwards. You don\'t have to worry, the display is&nbsp;&nbsp; relatively robust and as I showed in my Durability&nbsp; Test, it will survive quite a few drops. The new WindGuard is located on the front of&nbsp; the camera under the lens. This significantly&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reduces the wind noise and improves the&nbsp; audio quality of your shots. However,&nbsp;&nbsp; as it has a foam rubber inside, it is not&nbsp; waterproof, which is something you should&nbsp;&nbsp; be aware of. You can remove it by pushing it&nbsp; outwards from the side. If you want to use&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Ace Pro2 in water, you must replace the&nbsp; wind guard with this mic cap. It is included&nbsp;&nbsp; in every standard package. You press it in from&nbsp; the right and must make sure that no red stripe&nbsp;&nbsp; is visible - only then is the camera really&nbsp; waterproof. The Ace Pro 2 is waterproof up to&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '12 metres without an additional case.&nbsp; Nevertheless, especially in seawater,&nbsp;&nbsp; I would always recommend an additional case -&nbsp; the salt water will damage any camera in the long&nbsp;&nbsp; run if it is not cleaned properly after use. But&nbsp; for now, let\'s reattach the standard wind guard.'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There is one side door on the left and one on the&nbsp; right. The removable battery is located behind the&nbsp;&nbsp; left side door. Behind the right one is a USB-C&nbsp; port for charging the camera and connecting it&nbsp;&nbsp; to a PC - and an SD card slot. As you can see&nbsp; here, the right side door can also be easily&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'removed. To do this, simply push it upwards. For&nbsp; the Ace Pro 2 to be waterproof, both side doors&nbsp;&nbsp; must be completely closed. So always make sure&nbsp; that there is no orange stripe visible. Not all&nbsp;&nbsp; micro SD cards are suitable for the Ace Pro 2,&nbsp; especially if you also want to shoot in 8k or&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '4K120. You should use a UHS-I card with a speed&nbsp; rating of 3. This is a card from Insta360 - of&nbsp;&nbsp; course it works perfectly, but cards from other&nbsp; manufacturers such as the Sandisk Extreme or&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Extreme Pro are also suitable. By the way, you\'ll&nbsp; find links to all the accessories I\'m going to&nbsp;&nbsp; mention today in the video description. We have&nbsp; now removed the windguard and the right-hand side&nbsp;&nbsp; door. And fortunately, the lens cover is also very&nbsp; easy to remove and to replace if damaged. Simply&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'turn it to the left and you can then remove it.&nbsp; To reattach it, place it diagonally on the lens&nbsp;&nbsp; opening and turn it back in by turning it to the&nbsp; right. Let\'s take a quick look at the two buttons. In addition to the shutter button, the Ace Pro&nbsp; 2 also has a power or QuickSwitch button on the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'side. You can use this to switch the camera&nbsp; on and off and to switch the recording mode.&nbsp;&nbsp; You can even customise this button and assign&nbsp; important functions to it. I\'ll show you how&nbsp;&nbsp; to do this a little later. The removable magnetic&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mount is located on the underside. The mount can be removed by pressing&nbsp;&nbsp; it together on both sides. It only has very light&nbsp; magnets and is mainly attached to the camera by a&nbsp;&nbsp; locking mechanism. When it is properly attached,&nbsp; it is rock solid. To attach it, simply push it in.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The white camera symbol must be on the front. Make&nbsp; sure that the locking mechanism snaps in correctly&nbsp;&nbsp; and closes completely so that the camera is also&nbsp; attached correctly and cannot fall off. To be able&nbsp;&nbsp; to use the Ace Pro 2 effectively, you will need a&nbsp; number of mounts. One of the particular strengths&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of all Insta360 cameras, including the Ace Pro&nbsp; 2, is the large selection of high-quality mounts.&nbsp;&nbsp; You should definitely get some of them. To start&nbsp; with, I would definitely recommend a Pole. This&nbsp;&nbsp; multi mount, for example, is easy to fold up and&nbsp; thanks to the two hinges you can adjust it so that&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it is not visible in the shot. The handle can be&nbsp; unfolded so that the pole can also be used like&nbsp;&nbsp; a small tripod. If you want a slightly longer&nbsp; pole, I would recommend this pole from Insta360&nbsp;&nbsp; with a length of 114 cm. It is easy to store and&nbsp; has an optimal length. But be careful: you will&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'also need a tripod adapter to use this pole,&nbsp; as it does not have a traditional GoPro mount&nbsp;&nbsp; at the top. Then I would definitely recommend&nbsp; a floatable hangrip to use the Ace Pro 2 in the&nbsp;&nbsp; water. As I said, a dive case should definitely&nbsp; be considered for frequent use in salt water.&nbsp;'

[04:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And very important for me: a chest mount for&nbsp; POV shots when doing sports, so for example for&nbsp;&nbsp; biking or skiing. For me, a chest mount is part&nbsp; of the basic equipment of every action camera. Ok - Let\'s switch on the Ace Pro 2. You should&nbsp; connect your Ace Pro 2 to the smartphone app&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'right at the beginning. Once you have switched&nbsp; on the Ace Pro 2, tap on the camera symbol at&nbsp;&nbsp; the bottom centre of the Insta360 app and connect&nbsp; the camera. You have to activate your camera with&nbsp;&nbsp; the smartphone app the first time you use it and&nbsp; the smartphone app will also immediately show you&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whether an update is available. If an update&nbsp; is available, you should install the update,&nbsp;&nbsp; also because Insta360 not only fixes bugs via&nbsp; updates, but also keeps adding new features.&nbsp; The smartphone app from Insta360 is one&nbsp; of the great strengths of the Ace Pro 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'also because it offers a variety of useful&nbsp; features. Under Explore you will find tutorials,&nbsp;&nbsp; many videos, including videos by users and&nbsp; special offers, under Album you can view,&nbsp;&nbsp; edit and manage your shots and under Edit you&nbsp; will find many effects that you can apply to your&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shot and a complete tool to edit your videos.&nbsp; I\'ll show you the most important and coolest&nbsp;&nbsp; features included here at the end of the video. If you tap on the camera icon, you can see the&nbsp;&nbsp; preview image, start a recording, select the&nbsp; recording mode and change all the recording&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'settings using the icons here at the top and&nbsp; bottom. And we should now take a closer look&nbsp;&nbsp; at the recording modes and settings. But let\'s&nbsp; take a look at these directly on the camera. The Ace Pro 2 offers a wide range of features, but&nbsp; is still very easy to use. At the bottom left you&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can see the active recording mode that is video&nbsp; and the current settings so 4K30, at the top you&nbsp;&nbsp; can see the most important status information, at&nbsp; the bottom right the field of view, Mega and 1x&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stands for the Clarity Zoom. If you swipe up from&nbsp; the bottom, you can open the recording settings.&nbsp;&nbsp; You can also open these by simply tapping on&nbsp; the resolution and frame rate. Swiping from top&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to bottom opens the settings menu, where you can&nbsp; activate and deactivate individual features with&nbsp;&nbsp; a quick tap or open the main camera menu at the&nbsp; bottom right. If you swipe from left to right,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can see your last shot, open an overview of&nbsp; all your shots and also play them back. And if&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you swipe from the right edge to the left,&nbsp; you open the extended or advanced capture&nbsp;&nbsp; settings - here you can adjust the white balance&nbsp; or even set the exposure completely manually. Before we take a look at the different shooting&nbsp; modes, a few words about the Clarity Zoom,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as this is actually one of the&nbsp; special features of this camera.&nbsp; When you tap on the 1x, the camera zooms in by a&nbsp; factor of two. This also works while shooting. Of&nbsp;&nbsp; course, this is a digital crop, but not only.&nbsp; The high-resolution 50 megapixel sensor makes&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it possible to achieve an almost lossless zoom.&nbsp; But only almost - for the best image quality,&nbsp;&nbsp; you should still simply get closer if&nbsp; possible. But the result of the zoom&nbsp;&nbsp; is significantly better than if you were&nbsp; to crop the image in post-processing. So&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'use the Clarity Zoom directly when taking the&nbsp; shot if you can\'t get closer to the subject&nbsp;&nbsp; and want to take a close-up. The result will be&nbsp; much better than if you crop the image in post. The Ace Pro 2 offers a number of different&nbsp; shooting modes. You can change the shooting&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mode by swiping left or right in the centre of&nbsp; the display or by tapping on the icon with the&nbsp;&nbsp; shooting mode at the bottom left. Most recording&nbsp; modes, such as Video, Photo or Timelapse,&nbsp;&nbsp; are self-explanatory. You use Timeshift to create&nbsp; a hyperlapse. In this case, a kind of timelapse&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shot is taken and stabilised. In contrast to&nbsp; a timelapse shot, you use this mode when you&nbsp;&nbsp; are moving with the camera. I\'ll explain loop&nbsp; recording and the new dashcam mode a bit later.&nbsp;&nbsp; There are two recording modes, both of which are&nbsp; among the special and unique features of the Ace&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Pro 2 and which we should take a closer look at&nbsp; now. The Free Frame mode and the Pure Video mode. In freeframe video mode, basically the entire,&nbsp; uncropped and unstabilised image from the sensor&nbsp;&nbsp; is saved. This has a few decisive advantages: you&nbsp; can later freely select the image format in the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'smartphone or desktop app, i.e. whether&nbsp; you want a vertical or horizontal shot,&nbsp;&nbsp; and you can also freely select the field of view&nbsp; in post, i. in other words, whether you want your&nbsp;&nbsp; shot in the field of view Dewarp, Ultrawide&nbsp; or Actionview or Linear, and of course the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shot is then stabilised in the app. This means&nbsp; you must not set the correct field of view when&nbsp;&nbsp; taking the shot and you have more freedom when&nbsp; editing your clips. You can add artificial motion&nbsp;&nbsp; blur to your shot and the stabilisation&nbsp; should also be a little better than in&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'traditional video mode. These are many advantages. On the other hand, the Free Frame Video mode is&nbsp;&nbsp; only available in the maximum resolution of 4K,&nbsp; there are only frame rates of up to 60 frames per&nbsp;&nbsp; second and you have to edit each of your shots&nbsp; before you can use it, similar to a 360 camera.'

[09:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The Pure Video mode is one of the&nbsp; great strengths of the Ace Pro 2&nbsp;&nbsp; and is intended to deliver the best results in&nbsp; low light. In this video mode, the image noise&nbsp;&nbsp; caused by high ISO values is removed very&nbsp; efficiently. Especially in night scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Pure Video mode provides better colours, a&nbsp; better dynamic range and a clearer image than&nbsp;&nbsp; the normal video mode. You should therefore&nbsp; activate this mode in these situations&nbsp;&nbsp; and possibly also in artificial light indoors.&nbsp; The Pure Video mode supports frame rates of up&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to 60 frames per second. But especially when it&nbsp; is very dark, you should prefer a very low frame&nbsp;&nbsp; rate. A low frame rate is advantageous in low&nbsp; light because the camera can capture more light.&nbsp;&nbsp; This is why the recording mode is labelled Pure&nbsp; Video Plus if the frame rate is no higher than 30&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'frames per second. This is the only way to achieve&nbsp; the best results in very low light conditions. When you change the mode, you will see&nbsp; the preset field in the top right-hand&nbsp;&nbsp; corner. This means that once you have found&nbsp; the best settings for a particular situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can save them here as a preset and select&nbsp; them via this menu so that you must not change&nbsp;&nbsp; the settings manually each time. We will now&nbsp; take a look at the best settings for the Ace&nbsp;&nbsp; Pro 2 and save them as a preset. But before that,&nbsp; a few words about the QuickSwitch button. You can&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'also change the recording modes on the Ace Pro&nbsp; 2 using the button on the side, but in this case&nbsp;&nbsp; only the modes that have been selected for this&nbsp; purpose will appear, currently Video, Photo and&nbsp;&nbsp; Timelapse. If you tap on the three dots at the&nbsp; top right, you can add further modes and also&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your own presets. You should therefore add the&nbsp; modes and presets that you use frequently so that&nbsp;&nbsp; you can change the recording mode and settings&nbsp; even faster. A great feature. Now let\'s switch&nbsp;&nbsp; to the standard video mode and open the recording&nbsp; settings. So, what are the best recording settings&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for the Ace Pro 2? PAUSE In most cases, I would recommend a resolution&nbsp; of 4K. I would only recommend 8K in very special&nbsp;&nbsp; situations. A shot in 8K takes up significantly&nbsp; more storage space and is more difficult to&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'process. HDR is not available and only frame rates&nbsp; of up to 30 frames per second are available. But&nbsp;&nbsp; of course you can see the advantage of the&nbsp; higher resolution, especially in very good&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[11:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lighting conditions, and you can also crop the&nbsp; shot in post without a significant loss of image&nbsp;&nbsp; quality. I would therefore only recommend 8K if&nbsp; you want to watch your shots on a high-resolution&nbsp;&nbsp; screen and only for shots taken in very good&nbsp; lighting conditions. I use 4K as standard.&nbsp;'

[11:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Choosing the best frame rate is not that easy.&nbsp; Basically, a higher frame rate results in a&nbsp;&nbsp; shot that looks smoother and more fluid.&nbsp; I would therefore recommend a frame rate&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[11:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of 50 or 60 frames per second, especially&nbsp; for nature shots or sports. These frame&nbsp;&nbsp; rates produce the most natural look. Such a high frame rate has only one&nbsp;&nbsp; disadvantage - as already mentioned, it is not&nbsp; particularly suitable for shots in low light - and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[11:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in such a case you should not forget to use the&nbsp; Pure Video mode. And one more thing is important:&nbsp;&nbsp; if you want to create a longer video from several&nbsp; CLips, for example a holiday video, you should&nbsp;&nbsp; avoid mixing different frame rates of 24, 30 or&nbsp; 50 frames per second. This can lead to strange&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[12:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'results. You should therefore consider in advance&nbsp; at which frame rate you want to create your video.&nbsp; Incidentally, 25, 50 and 100 frames per&nbsp; second are intended for the PAL region,&nbsp;&nbsp; which would be most countries outside the USA&nbsp; and Canada. Frame rates of 30 or 60 frames per&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[12:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'second can lead to flickering problems&nbsp; in artificial light in these countries.&nbsp;&nbsp; What\'s new about the Ace Pro 2 is that it now&nbsp; supports up to 60 frames per second HDR mode,&nbsp;&nbsp; which is an important improvement, because the&nbsp; HDR feature of the Ace Pro 2 is a big advantage:&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[12:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it protects the highlights very well - even&nbsp; in very difficult lighting conditions they&nbsp;&nbsp; don\'t burn out. Imagine cycling through a shady&nbsp; forest - without HDR, the sky will burn out in&nbsp;&nbsp; such cases - no more details will be visible.&nbsp; That doesn\'t look good. Or even if the sun is&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[12:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'partially hidden behind the clouds, the HDR mode&nbsp; leads to better results. The HDR mode on the Ace&nbsp;&nbsp; Pro 2 never looks unrealistic or strange, as the&nbsp; highlights are protected but the shadows are not&nbsp;&nbsp; brightened. The shot still has enough contrast.&nbsp; For these reasons, I would always leave the Active&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[13:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'HDR mode activated. Some people are of the opinion&nbsp; that the HDR mode sometimes leads to unnatural&nbsp;&nbsp; results. I don\'t think this is the case with&nbsp; the Ace Pro 2 - but if you are of this opinion,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can deactivate it here. Especially for action&nbsp; shots or nature shots, I would recommend 60 frames&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[13:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'per second with HDR activated. 30 frames per&nbsp; second if the lighting conditions are not so good.&nbsp; 24 or 25 frames per second don\'t look as&nbsp; smooth and a choppy look is created when&nbsp;&nbsp; there is a lot of movement. However, this frame&nbsp; rate is considered particularly cinematic as&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[13:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it is used in professional movies. You should&nbsp; therefore only use this frame rate if your goal&nbsp;&nbsp; is to create a particularly cinematic look. For cool slow motion shots, I recommend 120&nbsp;&nbsp; frames per second. This allows you to create a&nbsp; slow motion of up to 20% - the quality is great&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[13:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and it looks very cool. For slow motion shots&nbsp; at 240 frames per second, you must reduce the&nbsp;&nbsp; resolution to 1080. But I wouldn\'t recommend that.&nbsp; The image quality will be significantly worse.&nbsp; When it comes to stabilisation, you can choose&nbsp; between Standard and High. In most cases, Standard&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[14:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is the better choice. High leads to slightly&nbsp; better stabilisation but also to a stronger&nbsp;&nbsp; crop. The wide field of view is a great advantage,&nbsp; especially for an action camera, and I wouldn\'t&nbsp;&nbsp; want to give up this advantage for a slightly&nbsp; better stabilisation. And I have found that&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[14:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'standard is completely sufficient in most cases,&nbsp; even for sports. Under Ratio you can select the&nbsp;&nbsp; image format, whereby it is interesting to note&nbsp; that Insta360 also offers a widescreen format of&nbsp;&nbsp; 2.35:1. You can use this format if you want your&nbsp; shots to have a particularly cinematic look. You&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[14:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can use Duration to set the Ace Pro 2 to end the&nbsp; recording automatically after a specified time.&nbsp; You can open the settings for the field of view&nbsp; by tapping the icon at the bottom right. You can&nbsp;&nbsp; choose between Actionview, Megaview, Ultrawide,&nbsp; Dewarp and Linear. Megaview is the standard field&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[14:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of view on the Ace Pro 2 and also the field&nbsp; of view that I usually use. It is very wide&nbsp;&nbsp; and the distortions of the fisheye lens are&nbsp; partially removed. If you want to reduce the&nbsp;&nbsp; distortion even further when vlogging or for&nbsp; shots in the city, for example, you can use&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[15:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Dewarp or even Linear to completely remove the&nbsp; distortion. In the case of Linear in particular,&nbsp;&nbsp; the field of view is heavily cropped, which I&nbsp; actually want to avoid. I use Actionview much&nbsp;&nbsp; more often than Dewarp or Linear. This is a&nbsp; particularly wide field of view. Especially&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[15:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'vertically, the field of view is significantly&nbsp; wider than with Ultrawide or Megaview. However,&nbsp;&nbsp; Actionview also has stronger distortions&nbsp; at the edges. Actionview is particularly&nbsp;&nbsp; suitable for POV shots, for example when skiing&nbsp; or biking with a chest mount or when filming&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[15:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'yourself with the pole during sport. The larger&nbsp; field of view means you simply get more in the&nbsp;&nbsp; frame. The Horizon Lock is also important for many&nbsp; people. If you activate one of these two options,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can turn the camera sideways, but the horizon&nbsp; always remains straight. This works up to a&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[15:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'rotation of 45° or even a complete 360° rotation.&nbsp; Of course, this results in a very stable shot, but&nbsp;&nbsp; also in a strong crop. My favourite settings are&nbsp; therefore Megaview or Actionview for POV shots.&nbsp;'

[16:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For the additional capture settings, swipe&nbsp; from the right edge to the left. Under M,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can set all exposure settings manually. I&nbsp; rarely do this with action cameras. However,&nbsp;&nbsp; we should take a closer look at the settings&nbsp; under Automatic. The first icon at the top left&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[16:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is for the colour profiles. In addition to the&nbsp; standard colour profile, which I usually use,&nbsp;&nbsp; there is also a colour profile with more&nbsp; saturation called Vivid. I find this a bit&nbsp;&nbsp; too much in most cases. Apart from that, the&nbsp; Ace Pro 2 also offers you a range of special&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[16:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'looks for very specific situations. For example,&nbsp; a colour profile for portrait shots, Urban for&nbsp;&nbsp; vlogging shots in the city or Night for night&nbsp; shots. Apart from the standard colour profile,&nbsp;&nbsp; I would also like to recommend Leica Natural.&nbsp; This is a very high-contrast and cinematic colour&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[16:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'profile from the camera manufacturer Leica. If&nbsp; you want to colour grade your shots yourself,&nbsp;&nbsp; you should activate I-Log here on the right. This&nbsp; is a flat log profile that is ideal for colour&nbsp;&nbsp; grading. On the Insta360 website, you can download&nbsp; a lut that automatically converts I-Log shots into&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[17:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shots with a conventional look. Personally, I&nbsp; rarely use it, and as I said, I would recommend&nbsp;&nbsp; the standard profile to start with. Under EV you can determine whether the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[17:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'automatic exposure should expose the shot a little&nbsp; brighter or darker. The Ace Pro 2 usually exposes&nbsp;&nbsp; the shot correctly and well - the HDR mode also&nbsp; prevents burnt-out highlights. On the other hand,&nbsp;&nbsp; if you are filming without HDR, you can consider&nbsp; setting a slightly negative value of perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[17:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '-0.3 or -0.7 to prevent burnt-out highlights.&nbsp; Shadows can be brightened up relatively easily in&nbsp;&nbsp; post-processing. But burnt-out highlights can no&nbsp; longer be corrected in post. The details are lost.&nbsp; Here on the right you can set the white balance&nbsp; manually. On the Ace Pro 2, the automatic mode&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[17:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'works very well. I therefore rarely use this&nbsp; feature. You can set the white balance manually&nbsp;&nbsp; if you want to prevent the camera\'s automatic&nbsp; mode from changing the white balance during a&nbsp;&nbsp; longer shot for no apparent reason. On a sunny&nbsp; day, for example, you can use 5000 or 5400.&nbsp;'

[18:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In the standard settings, the automatic exposure&nbsp; is based on your face - you can recognise this by&nbsp;&nbsp; the yellow frame. This usually works well, but&nbsp; sometimes the shot will be a little bright. If&nbsp;&nbsp; this bothers you and you want the entire scene&nbsp; to be taken into account, select Matrix here. In&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[18:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'low light conditions, the automatic exposure&nbsp; will reduce the shutter speed to let in more&nbsp;&nbsp; light. However, this leads to more motion blur&nbsp; and consequently to poorer image stabilisation,&nbsp;&nbsp; which can result in some jittering. If you also&nbsp; need a particularly well-stabilised image in low&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[18:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'light, you should activate Jitter Blur Reduction&nbsp; here. But be careful - this will have a negative&nbsp;&nbsp; effect on the image quality and can also darken&nbsp; the shot. And don\'t forget to use the Pure Video&nbsp;&nbsp; Mode in Low Light. The same feature is of&nbsp; course also available there. At the bottom&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[18:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'there is another very important setting - Video&nbsp; Sharpness. Every consumer camera will artificially&nbsp;&nbsp; increase the contrast at the edges. This makes&nbsp; a shot look sharper and more detailed at first&nbsp;&nbsp; glance. Unfortunately, however, it also looks&nbsp; more digital and not very professional. I would&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[19:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'therefore never set the sharpness higher than&nbsp; medium, but rather reduce it to low. However,&nbsp;&nbsp; a shot taken with Low can look very soft and it&nbsp; may be necessary to add sharpness in post. If&nbsp;&nbsp; you don\'t want to do this and want to use the&nbsp; shot directly, then use a sharpness of Medium.&nbsp;'

[19:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'We have now discussed the recording&nbsp; settings in the standard video mode,&nbsp;&nbsp; but the other recording modes&nbsp; also have these setting options,&nbsp;&nbsp; whereby individual options are of&nbsp; course omitted depending on the mode.'

[19:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you have now set up your Ace Pro 2 properly,&nbsp; for the best image quality you should also&nbsp;&nbsp; consider another setting in the main menu. To do&nbsp; this, I swipe down from the top edge and open the&nbsp;&nbsp; settings menu. There is an important setting here&nbsp; under image settings. For the best image quality,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[19:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you should make sure that the bit rate is set&nbsp; to High. Although this results in larger files,&nbsp;&nbsp; it is the only way to store as much image&nbsp; information as possible. I would only use Standard&nbsp;&nbsp; if you absolutely have to save storage space, for&nbsp; example if you are on a long trip. In this menu&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[20:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you will also find the general camera settings -&nbsp; you can set the language and date here or format&nbsp;&nbsp; the SD card. There are also a few very special&nbsp; features here that I will show you a little later. Once you have set up the Ace Pro 2 perfectly, open&nbsp; the menu with the recording modes, select Preset&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[20:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and then the plus on the far right. You can now&nbsp; save your current settings under one of the preset&nbsp;&nbsp; names and can also make further changes here via&nbsp; edit. Don\'t forget to save your preset at the end.&nbsp; Ok, it\'s time to start a recording, then I can&nbsp; show you some very cool and special features of&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[20:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Ace Pro 2. PAUSE When you have started a recording, you can not&nbsp; only activate the 2x zoom during the shot using&nbsp;&nbsp; the clarity zoom, you can also manually add a&nbsp; highlight by tapping the flag at the bottom right&nbsp;&nbsp; to make it easier to find the moment in the shot&nbsp; later. You can take photos during video recording&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[20:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'via the icon with the circle. And particularly&nbsp; interesting: you can pause the shot with a tap,&nbsp;&nbsp; possibly change the framing, maybe even change&nbsp; the field of view and then you can resume the&nbsp;&nbsp; shot with another tap or by pressing the shutter&nbsp; button. The entire shot is then saved in the same&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[21:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'file. If you have paused the shot and then want&nbsp; to stop it, tap the red square at the bottom&nbsp;&nbsp; right. And if you realise during the recording&nbsp; that the shot has failed and is not usable,&nbsp;&nbsp; press and hold the shutter button. The shot will&nbsp; now be deleted immediately. This saves time and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[21:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the failed shot doesn\'t take up any memory space.&nbsp; And another absolutely cool feature - you can even&nbsp;&nbsp; resume an existing, older shot. To do this,&nbsp; open the overview of your clips, select a&nbsp;&nbsp; clip and tap on the small icon at the bottom&nbsp; right - now this exact shot will be resumed.'

[21:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'We have now mainly focused on the Video and the&nbsp; Pure Video mode: However, with Loop Recording&nbsp;&nbsp; and Dashcam mode, you can also use the Ace Pro&nbsp; 2 for very specific purposes. You should use&nbsp;&nbsp; Loop Recording if you want to use the Ace Pro 2&nbsp; as a bodycam, for example. You set a recording&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[21:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'duration, for example 3 or 5 minutes, and your&nbsp; Ace Pro 2 will record continuously after the&nbsp;&nbsp; recording has started. However, only the last 3 or&nbsp; 5 minutes after you have stopped the recording are&nbsp;&nbsp; saved. And you should always stop the recording&nbsp; when something important has happened. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[22:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this can also be interesting for certain sports.&nbsp; The dashcam mode works in a very similar way,&nbsp;&nbsp; except that the limiting factor&nbsp; here is not a number of minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp; but a certain amount of memory on your memory&nbsp; card - as you can charge the camera for example&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[22:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in the car while recording, you can capture&nbsp; loops of several hours, whereby the oldest&nbsp;&nbsp; recordings are always overwritten. This way you&nbsp; can be sure that important moments are saved. Before we take a look at the best effects and&nbsp; features of the app, I have to show you a few&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[22:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'important additional camera features. To do&nbsp; this, swipe down from the top edge. Here you&nbsp;&nbsp; can switch several important features on and off&nbsp; with a simple tap. Most of these are important&nbsp;&nbsp; but typical features of action cameras. But&nbsp; three features in particular are unique to the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[22:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Ace Pro 2: the AI Highlights Assistant, Gesture&nbsp; Control and the new audio settings. But first a&nbsp;&nbsp; few words about the other features, as these are&nbsp; also very useful. If you activate QuickCapture,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[23:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can start a shot by pressing the shutter&nbsp; button when the Ace Pro 2 is switched off. You&nbsp;&nbsp; should use this as often as possible to save time&nbsp; and battery. If you turn the Ace Pro 2 sideways,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can take a shot in portrait mode, for example&nbsp; for social media. Unfortunately, this can also&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[23:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'happen unintentionally if you have mounted your&nbsp; Ace Pro 2 on a selfie stick and then start a shot.&nbsp;&nbsp; This can be annoying and unfortunately&nbsp; happens to me all the time. To prevent this,&nbsp;&nbsp; you should activate the orientation lock. If&nbsp; you activate pre-recording, the 15, 30 or 60&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[23:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'seconds before you press the shutter button are&nbsp; also saved. This is to prevent you from missing&nbsp;&nbsp; an important moment, for example when fishing. Of&nbsp; course, the Ace Pro 2 must shoot continuously for&nbsp;&nbsp; this. This requires battery power - so only&nbsp; use this feature when you really need it.'

[23:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'On the other hand, if you must save battery&nbsp; power and want to take very long shots,&nbsp;&nbsp; you should activate the Endurance&nbsp; mode. It will significantly extend&nbsp;&nbsp; the battery life of your Ace Pro 2. You&nbsp; can shoot in 4K30 for more than 2 hours,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[24:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'although some features are not available here. If you use the Ace Pro 2 underwater, you should&nbsp;&nbsp; activate the underwater mode. The stabilisation&nbsp; and distortion, but also the colours, are adapted&nbsp;&nbsp; to shots under water. Unfortunately, I can\'t show&nbsp; you an example because the nearest ocean is too&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[24:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'far away. Here you can lock the display and&nbsp; the grid should help you with the composition&nbsp;&nbsp; of your shots. So that you can stick&nbsp; to the Rule of Thirds, for example.&nbsp; The Ace Pro 2 also supports voice control and&nbsp; commands such as Start Recording, Stop Recording&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[24:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or Take a Photo. This can be very useful if you&nbsp; want to start a shot from a distance, for example.&nbsp; You can use this icon to adjust the&nbsp; brightness of the display and the icon&nbsp;&nbsp; at the bottom left to schedule a shot. This is&nbsp; interesting for a timelapse shot, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[24:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'if you don\'t want to get up in the morning but&nbsp; want to capture the sunrise. Also cool - you can&nbsp;&nbsp; use this feature to attach the camera somewhere&nbsp; and automatically take a photo every day - so you&nbsp;&nbsp; can take a long-term timelapse, for example. The Ace Pro 2 can not only be connected to&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[25:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your Apple Watch and your Garmin to save the most&nbsp; important data such as GPS, Insta360 also offers&nbsp;&nbsp; two different remote controls in the form of a&nbsp; wristband. The GPS Preview Remote is certainly&nbsp;&nbsp; one of the most useful accessories for the Ace&nbsp; Pro 2. It not only stores the GPS data, it also&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[25:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'has a full touch display with which you can check&nbsp; the framing. This is particularly useful if you&nbsp;&nbsp; have mounted your Ace Pro 2 on a helmet. You will&nbsp; find a link to it in the video description. It is&nbsp;&nbsp; also possible to capture the GPS data without a&nbsp; remote - I\'ll show you how to do this a bit later.'

[25:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The Ace Pro 2 can also be connected to Airpods&nbsp; and you can then use the Airpods as an external&nbsp;&nbsp; microphone. A useful feature if you have the&nbsp; camera mounted on the outside of your car,&nbsp;&nbsp; for example - even if you shouldn\'t expect&nbsp; too much from the audio quality. But&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[25:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'let\'s move on to the three very special&nbsp; features of the Ace Pro 2 in this menu: The Ace Pro 2 not only supports voice control,&nbsp; but also gesture control. If you activate this&nbsp;&nbsp; feature, you can start a recording by simply&nbsp; moving your hand. You can stop the recording&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[26:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'again with another hand gesture. You can&nbsp; take a photo with the peace sign. And it&nbsp;&nbsp; works surprisingly well, even when wearing&nbsp; gloves. This feature is always useful when&nbsp;&nbsp; voice control is not suitable, for example because&nbsp; it is too windy or the Ace Pro 2 is too far away.'

[26:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The first Ace Pro already owed its reputation&nbsp; as an AI action camera to the AI Highlights&nbsp;&nbsp; Assistant. But what can this assistant actually&nbsp; do? I don\'t think we all want to spend hours&nbsp;&nbsp; searching through videos for interesting moments&nbsp; and waste a lot of time editing videos. The goal&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[26:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'would be for this work to be done directly by the&nbsp; AI. To do this, however, the camera must recognise&nbsp;&nbsp; which moments in the video are interesting and&nbsp; valuable, and that\'s where the AI Highlights&nbsp;&nbsp; assistant comes in. It recognises subjects and&nbsp; can identify important moments in the shot and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[26:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mark them as highlights. All of this is done in&nbsp; the camera and not via the app. This saves time&nbsp;&nbsp; and the app must not analyse the shot again. When&nbsp; you open your clips in the camera, you can see in&nbsp;&nbsp; the overview whether highlights have been added&nbsp; to the respective clip based on the flag and the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[27:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'number. If you then open the individual clip, you&nbsp; can view your highlights by tapping on the flag&nbsp;&nbsp; icon. You can now delete individual highlights and&nbsp; manually add more highlights yourself. It is also&nbsp;&nbsp; useful that you can save your highlights directly&nbsp; in a new clip. To do this, tap on the disc icon&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[27:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'at the top right, select the best highlights&nbsp; and then choose whether you want to create a&nbsp;&nbsp; separate clip for each highlight or whether you&nbsp; want to combine all selected highlights into a&nbsp;&nbsp; single clip. This feature is particularly useful&nbsp; if you have very long clips that take up a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[27:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'memory. You can quickly save the most important&nbsp; parts in a new file and delete the original long&nbsp;&nbsp; clip. You should also know that the Highlights&nbsp; Assistant requires a relatively large amount&nbsp;&nbsp; of power. Therefore, if you want to extend the&nbsp; battery life, you should deactivate this feature.'

[27:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And as already shown at the beginning, the Ace&nbsp; Pro 2 is supposed to take the audio quality&nbsp;&nbsp; of your shots to a new level and finally avoid&nbsp; annoying wind noise thanks to the new Windguard.&nbsp;&nbsp; Under Audio Input Device, you can not only&nbsp; connect an external microphone via Bluetooth,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[28:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can also set the audio settings, for example&nbsp; to Wind Reduction or Voice Enhancement, whereby&nbsp;&nbsp; background noise is filtered out particularly&nbsp; efficiently. This is an excellent feature,&nbsp;&nbsp; especially for vlogging. As you can see, the Ace&nbsp; Pro 2 has a large number of useful features. And&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[28:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'before we transfer our shots and take a look&nbsp; at the app, I must show you something else. In the settings menu at the bottom right, you can&nbsp; deactivate the rather conspicuous led lights or&nbsp;&nbsp; adjust the volume of the sounds. You can activate&nbsp; the timecode here when using multiple cameras and,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[28:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'very interestingly, you can customise the&nbsp; power button to suit your needs. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp; if you find that you rarely change the&nbsp; recording mode, you can also use the&nbsp;&nbsp; power button to switch the screen on and&nbsp; off or activate the clarity zoom or even&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[28:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to activate the pause function during a shot.&nbsp; One of the many cool features of this camera. There are several ways to store and transfer&nbsp; your clips. You can of course remove the SD&nbsp;&nbsp; card and transfer the files to your computer.&nbsp; You can connect the Ace Pro 2 to your PC using&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[28:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a USB-C cable and, of course, you can also&nbsp; transfer your shots to your smartphone. And&nbsp;&nbsp; it\'s in this context that I\'d like to show you the&nbsp; first special feature of the smartphone app. Once&nbsp;&nbsp; you have connected your camera, select Album and&nbsp; tap the checkmark in the top right-hand corner.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[29:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Now you can select several clips and download&nbsp; them to your smartphone or export them in a&nbsp;&nbsp; different resolution or frame rate. The cool&nbsp; thing is that it all runs in the background.&nbsp;&nbsp; You can select several files for download,&nbsp; start the download and then close the app&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[29:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and use your smartphone for other purposes.&nbsp; You will receive a notification as soon as&nbsp;&nbsp; the download is complete. And that\'s not the&nbsp; only special feature of the app, of course.&nbsp; The app has another unique feature.&nbsp; If you switch to the recording screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[29:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as described at the beginning, you can change&nbsp; all the camera settings here. And if you tap on&nbsp;&nbsp; the 3 dots at the top right, another menu opens.&nbsp; And extremely useful: if you activate GPS here,&nbsp;&nbsp; all GPS data captured by your smartphone will be&nbsp; transferred to the recording. So you no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[29:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'need a remote to capture the GPS data and can add&nbsp; the speed, distance or route to your shot. You can&nbsp;&nbsp; do this in the album by adding the stats. This is&nbsp; a very clever solution. Under edit you will find Under Creative you will find several options for&nbsp; editing your videos. If you tap on the Create a&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[30:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Video button, a complete video editing program&nbsp; opens where you can also add titles, music and&nbsp;&nbsp; effects to your shots. If you don\'t feel like&nbsp; editing your videos manually, you can use the Auto&nbsp;&nbsp; Edit feature. Here you simply select the clips you&nbsp; want to use and the app will automatically compile&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[30:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a short clip, add music, a title, transitions&nbsp; and effects. As far as the look is concerned,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can also select one of many templates&nbsp; below. Try it out - it works surprisingly well.&nbsp; Under Flash Cut and Shot Lab you will find a&nbsp; variety of interesting effects that you can&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[30:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'apply to your videos to quickly create&nbsp; short interesting clips. Today I would&nbsp;&nbsp; like to show you two effects under Shot Lab that&nbsp; are particularly interesting for the Ace Pro 2:&nbsp; AI Warp applies an AI-generated effect to your&nbsp; clip. To do this, you select one or more clips.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[30:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If the duration of the clip is longer than 15&nbsp; seconds, tap on the clip at the bottom left&nbsp;&nbsp; and select a part of your clip. Confirm with the&nbsp; check mark. A maximum length of 4 seconds is also&nbsp;&nbsp; selected here. You can now decide whether the&nbsp; effect should be applied to the entire image or&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[31:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just a part of the image. For example, if the&nbsp; effect is only to be applied to the subject,&nbsp;&nbsp; select Custom and then select your subject.&nbsp; Then confirm your selection. Under Style,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can then select a style for the effect, for&nbsp; example Sci-Fi. Before the video is created,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[31:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you should watch the preview. This allows you&nbsp; to try out several styles and then select the&nbsp;&nbsp; best style for the video. And particularly&nbsp; interesting: you can influence the style&nbsp;&nbsp; of the effect yourself by entering text via&nbsp; the plus button under Custom. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[31:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I write Desert with orange sand. Similar&nbsp; to Dall-E or Midjourney, the AI will then&nbsp;&nbsp; generate the effect based on your text input.&nbsp; When you are finished, tap on Make AI Video.&nbsp;&nbsp; Your clip will now be uploaded and you can use&nbsp; your smartphone for other purposes. You can find&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[31:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the finished clip later under edit if you tap&nbsp; on the icon at the top right with the clock. And of course, I still have to show you how&nbsp; to remove the selfie stick from the clip. You&nbsp;&nbsp; can also find this feature under ShotLab.&nbsp; It\'s called AI selfie stick eraser. The&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[32:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'feature is very simple: you select your&nbsp; clip with the selfie stick, tap next,&nbsp;&nbsp; set the length - it can be a maximum&nbsp; of 120 seconds - and tap next again.&nbsp; For this feature you may not close the app during&nbsp; processing, but it is quite fast and works great,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[32:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even if the result is not saved in&nbsp; full resolution, but only in 1080.&nbsp; I think you now know everything you need to take&nbsp; excellent shots with your Ace Pro 2. I wish you&nbsp;&nbsp; lots of fun with your camera. Give me a like&nbsp; as feedback if you found the video interesting.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[32:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There will be more videos and tutorials on the&nbsp; Ace Pro 2, so stay tuned and see you next time!'
